{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"neopixel","name":"NeoPixel LEDs (WS2812B)","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Addressable RGB LEDs (WS2812B, \"NeoPixels\"): a stick of 8, a strip of 30 and an 8x8 panel. One data wire sets every LED's colour; chain them DOUT to DIN. Includes Adafruit_NeoPixel.h.","category":"Displays","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// WS2812B LEDs. A real strip takes a fast train of bits on DIN: each LED keeps the first 24 bits\n// (green, red, blue) and passes the rest on to the next. Here that train arrives as one message\n// ('pixels': G, R, B bytes for LED 0, 1, 2...); what's left over goes out of DOUT to the next strip.\nbench.device('ws2812', (part) => {\n  const screen = part.screen('leds');\n  const n = screen.cols * screen.rows;\n  const zigzag = !!part.params.zigzag;\n  const leds = new Array(n).fill(null).map(() => [0, 0, 0]);\n  let powered = false, frames = 0, amps = 0, lastLen = 0, rest = null;\n\n  // how bright an LED looks: even a dim one glows clearly, so show low values a bit brighter\n  const look = (v) => Math.round(255 * Math.pow(v / 255, 0.5));\n  const draw = () => {\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      let x = i % screen.cols, y = Math.floor(i / screen.cols);\n      if (zigzag && y % 2 === 1) x = screen.cols - 1 - x;\n      const [r, g, b] = powered ? leds[i] : [0, 0, 0];\n      screen.set(x, y, r || g || b ? `rgb(${look(r)},${look(g)},${look(b)})` : 0);\n    }\n  };\n  return {\n    packets(list) {\n      for (const p of list) {\n        if (p.pin !== 'DIN' || p.proto !== 'pixels' || !powered) continue;\n        const d = p.data;\n        lastLen = d.length;\n        for (let i = 0; i < n && i * 3 + 2 < d.length; i++) leds[i] = [d[i * 3 + 1], d[i * 3], d[i * 3 + 2]]; // (G, R, B on the wire)\n        frames++;\n        if (d.length > n * 3) rest = d.slice(n * 3);\n      }\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const now = io.supply('5V', 'GND') >= 3.5;\n      if (now !== powered) {\n        powered = now;\n        if (!now) for (const l of leds) l.fill(0); // (they forget their colours without power)\n      }\n      if (rest) {\n        io.send('DOUT', 'pixels', rest);\n        rest = null;\n      }\n      // each colour of each LED takes up to 20 mA at full brightness, plus about 1 mA for its chip\n      let sum = 0;\n      for (const [r, g, b] of leds) sum += r + g + b;\n      amps = powered ? (sum / 255) * 0.02 + n * 0.001 : 0;\n      io.draw(amps);\n      draw();\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (5V)'];\n      const lit = leds.filter(([r, g, b]) => r || g || b).length;\n      return [`${lit} of ${n} lit, ${frames} updates, ${(amps * 1000).toFixed(0)} mA`, ...(lastLen && lastLen < n * 3 ? [`the last update set only ${Math.floor(lastLen / 3)} LEDs`] : [])];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"Adafruit_NeoPixel.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_NeoPixel"],"exports":["NEO_RGB","NEO_RBG","NEO_GRB","NEO_GBR","NEO_BRG","NEO_BGR","NEO_KHZ800","NEO_KHZ400"],"code":"// Adafruit_NeoPixel for sketches: Adafruit_NeoPixel strip(count, pin, NEO_GRB + NEO_KHZ800);\n// begin(), setPixelColor(i, r, g, b) or (i, color), show(), clear(), fill(), setBrightness(),\n// Color(r, g, b), ColorHSV(hue, sat, val), gamma32(), numPixels(). show() sends every LED's colour\n// along the data wire as one message (what a real strip gets as a fast stream of bits).\nconst NEO_RGB = 0x06, NEO_RBG = 0x09, NEO_GRB = 0x52, NEO_GBR = 0xa1, NEO_BRG = 0x58, NEO_BGR = 0xa4, NEO_KHZ800 = 0x0000, NEO_KHZ400 = 0x0100;\n\nclass Adafruit_NeoPixel {\n  constructor(n = 0, pin = -1, type = NEO_GRB + NEO_KHZ800) {\n    this.n = n;\n    this.pin = pin;\n    this.type = type;\n    this.pixels = new Array(n * 3).fill(0); // r, g, b per LED (as set)\n    this.brightness = 0; // 0 = full (as the real library stores it)\n    this.begun = false;\n  }\n  begin() {\n    if (this.pin >= 0) {\n      pinMode(this.pin, OUTPUT);\n      digitalWrite(this.pin, LOW);\n    }\n    this.begun = true;\n  }\n  updateLength(n) { this.n = n; this.pixels = new Array(n * 3).fill(0); }\n  setPin(p) { this.pin = p; if (this.begun) this.begin(); }\n  numPixels() { return this.n; }\n  static Color(r, g, b, w) { return ((r & 255) << 16) | ((g & 255) << 8) | (b & 255); }\n  Color(r, g, b, w) { return Adafruit_NeoPixel.Color(r, g, b, w); }\n  setPixelColor(i, r, g, b) {\n    if (i < 0 || i >= this.n) return;\n    if (g === undefined) { const c = r >>> 0; b = c & 255; g = (c >> 8) & 255; r = (c >> 16) & 255; }\n    this.pixels[i * 3] = r & 255;\n    this.pixels[i * 3 + 1] = g & 255;\n    this.pixels[i * 3 + 2] = b & 255;\n  }\n  getPixelColor(i) {\n    if (i < 0 || i >= this.n) return 0;\n    return Adafruit_NeoPixel.Color(this.pixels[i * 3], this.pixels[i * 3 + 1], this.pixels[i * 3 + 2]);\n  }\n  fill(c = 0, first = 0, count = 0) {\n    const end = count ? Math.min(this.n, first + count) : this.n;\n    for (let i = first; i < end; i++) this.setPixelColor(i, c);\n  }\n  clear() { this.pixels.fill(0); }\n  setBrightness(b) { this.brightness = ((b & 255) + 1) & 255; }\n  getBrightness() { return (this.brightness - 1) & 255; }\n  canShow() { return true; }\n  show() {\n    if (this.pin < 0) return;\n    // the bytes in wire order (GRB for the usual LEDs), scaled by the brightness\n    const order = this.type & 0xff;\n    const rOff = (order >> 4) & 3, gOff = (order >> 2) & 3, bOff = order & 3;\n    const out = new Array(this.n * 3).fill(0);\n    for (let i = 0; i < this.n; i++) {\n      let r = this.pixels[i * 3], g = this.pixels[i * 3 + 1], b = this.pixels[i * 3 + 2];\n      if (this.brightness) {\n        r = (r * this.brightness) >> 8;\n        g = (g * this.brightness) >> 8;\n        b = (b * this.brightness) >> 8;\n      }\n      out[i * 3 + rOff] = r;\n      out[i * 3 + gOff] = g;\n      out[i * 3 + bOff] = b;\n    }\n    linkSend(this.pin, 'pixels', out);\n  }\n  static ColorHSV(hue = 0, sat = 255, val = 255) {\n    hue = ((hue % 65536) + 65536) % 65536;\n    hue = Math.floor((hue * 1530 + 32768) / 65536);\n    let r, g, b;\n    if (hue < 510) { b = 0; if (hue < 255) { r = 255; g = hue; } else { r = 510 - hue; g = 255; } }\n    else if (hue < 1020) { r = 0; if (hue < 765) { g = 255; b = hue - 510; } else { g = 1020 - hue; b = 255; } }\n    else if (hue < 1530) { g = 0; if (hue < 1275) { r = hue - 1020; b = 255; } else { r = 255; b = 1530 - hue; } }\n    else { r = 255; g = 0; b = 0; }\n    const v1 = 1 + val, s1 = 1 + sat, s2 = 255 - sat;\n    return Adafruit_NeoPixel.Color(((((r * s1) >> 8) + s2) * v1) >> 8, ((((g * s1) >> 8) + s2) * v1) >> 8, ((((b * s1) >> 8) + s2) * v1) >> 8);\n  }\n  ColorHSV(h, s, v) { return Adafruit_NeoPixel.ColorHSV(h, s, v); }\n  static gamma8(x) { return Math.round(Math.pow((x & 255) / 255, 2.6) * 255); }\n  static gamma32(c) {\n    return Adafruit_NeoPixel.Color(Adafruit_NeoPixel.gamma8(c >> 16), Adafruit_NeoPixel.gamma8(c >> 8), Adafruit_NeoPixel.gamma8(c));\n  }\n  gamma32(c) { return Adafruit_NeoPixel.gamma32(c); }\n  rainbow(first = 0, reps = 1, sat = 255, bright = 255, gammify = true) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < this.n; i++) {\n      const c = Adafruit_NeoPixel.ColorHSV(first + Math.floor((i * reps * 65536) / this.n), sat, bright);\n      this.setPixelColor(i, gammify ? Adafruit_NeoPixel.gamma32(c) : c);\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"stick8","name":"NeoPixel stick (8 LEDs)","description":"8 WS2812B LEDs in a row. 5V and GND (each LED takes up to 60 mA at full white), DIN to a pin. Adafruit_NeoPixel strip(8, PIN, NEO_GRB + NEO_KHZ800);","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":3,"params":[{"key":"count","label":"LEDs","kind":"number","min":8,"max":8,"step":1}],"defaults":{"count":8},"shape":[{"box":[5.1,0.16,1],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"screen":{"id":"leds","size":[4.8,0.6],"px":[8,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ffffff","off":"#e8e4dc","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0,0.17,0]}],"pins":[{"id":"DIN","at":[-2.4,0.16,0.381],"kind":"in"},{"id":"5V","label":"5V (4-5.5 V)","at":[-2.4,0.16,0.127],"kind":"vin","vmin":3.5,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-2.4,0.16,-0.127],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"DOUT","at":[2.4,0.16,0.381],"kind":"out"}],"device":"ws2812"},{"id":"strip30","name":"NeoPixel strip (30 LEDs)","description":"Half a metre of WS2812B strip, 30 LEDs. Give it its own 5 V supply for bright colours (30 LEDs at full white take 1.8 A); share its GND with the board. DIN to a pin.","swatch":"#f2f2f2","mass":20,"params":[{"key":"count","label":"LEDs","kind":"number","min":30,"max":30,"step":1}],"defaults":{"count":30},"shape":[{"box":[50,0.1,1],"at":[0,0.05,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"screen":{"id":"leds","size":[49.5,0.55],"px":[30,1],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ffffff","off":"#e8e4dc","bg":"#f2f2f2"},"at":[0,0.11,0]}],"pins":[{"id":"DIN","at":[-25,0.1,0.3],"kind":"in"},{"id":"5V","label":"5V (4-5.5 V)","at":[-25,0.1,0],"kind":"vin","vmin":3.5,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-25,0.1,-0.3],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"DOUT","at":[25,0.1,0.3],"kind":"out"}],"device":"ws2812"},{"id":"matrix8x8","name":"NeoPixel panel (8x8)","description":"64 WS2812B LEDs in an 8x8 grid, row by row from the top left (LED 0) to the bottom right (LED 63). 5V, GND, DIN. Needs a good 5 V supply for bright colours (up to 3.8 A).","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":25,"params":[{"key":"count","label":"LEDs","kind":"number","min":64,"max":64,"step":1},{"key":"zigzag","label":"Rows zig-zag (every other row backwards)","kind":"bool"}],"defaults":{"count":64,"zigzag":false},"shape":[{"box":[6.5,0.16,6.5],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"screen":{"id":"leds","size":[6.2,6.2],"px":[8,8],"mode":"pixels","on":"#ffffff","off":"#e8e4dc","bg":"#1a1a1c"},"at":[0,0.17,0]}],"pins":[{"id":"DIN","at":[-3.3,0.16,0.381],"kind":"in"},{"id":"5V","label":"5V (4-5.5 V)","at":[-3.3,0.16,0.127],"kind":"vin","vmin":3.5,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-3.3,0.16,-0.127],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"DOUT","at":[3.3,0.16,0.381],"kind":"out"}],"device":"ws2812"}],"examples":[{"name":"Rainbow stick","description":"A board sending a moving rainbow to an 8-LED stick with Adafruit_NeoPixel. Press Run.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Rainbow stick","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-6,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"stick","type":"neopixel/stick8","name":"LED stick","params":{"count":8},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"DIN"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"5V"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"stick","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// A moving rainbow on 8 NeoPixels.\n#include <Adafruit_NeoPixel.h>\n\n#define PIN 6\n#define COUNT 8\n\nAdafruit_NeoPixel strip(COUNT, PIN, NEO_GRB + NEO_KHZ800);\nlong hue = 0;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  strip.begin();\n  strip.setBrightness(80);   // of 255: easy on the eyes (and the USB port)\n  strip.show();              // all off\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  for (int i = 0; i < COUNT; i++) {\n    long h = hue + (long)i * 65536 / COUNT;\n    strip.setPixelColor(i, strip.gamma32(strip.ColorHSV(h)));\n  }\n  strip.show();\n  hue += 512;\n  delay(20);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}